{#-
  BLOCK: signature — §06's `signature`. The platform footer: wordmark, postal
  address, unsubscribe.

  Invariant across all eight report types, and the most legally loaded twelve
  lines in the product.

  #6b7280 AND NOT #9ca3af, ON ALL THREE LINES. D-060 raised the postal address
  off #9ca3af — 2.41:1 on this #f8f9fa panel, failing AA at 4.5 and failing the
  large-text allowance at 3.0 too, at 10px — and NAMED the unsubscribe link as
  the thing it was matching, then left it there. CAN-SPAM asks for the opt-out to
  be clear and conspicuous on the same wording that drove the address. All three
  are 4.59:1 now.

  `postal_address_html` arrives pre-rendered because whether the line appears,
  and whose address it carries, is decided in Python: an account's own address
  when set, the platform's otherwise, with a label saying which. A wrong address
  is an affirmative false statement rather than a missing one, so that choice
  does not belong in a template.
-#}
          <!-- ========== POWERED BY + UNSUBSCRIBE ========== -->
          <tr>
            <td style="background-color: #f8f9fa; padding: 16px 28px; border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; text-align: center;">
              <p style="margin: 0 0 4px 0; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; color: #6b7280;">
                Powered by <span style="font-weight: 600; color: #6b7280;">TrendyReports</span>
              </p>
{{ postal_address_html }}              <p style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Outfit', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; color: #6b7280;">
                <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color: #6b7280; text-decoration: underline;">Unsubscribe</a>
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
